  "slug": "the-pane-header-and-the-info-bar-come-out-of-chrome-mod-rs",
  "title": "The pane header and the info bar come out of chrome/mod.rs",
  "discussedAt": "",
  "contextReady": false,
  "contextReadyReason": "",
  "summary": "Extract the header (title + action buttons) and the segment bar (icons + text + overflow) into components, deleting the hand-rolled measure and truncation with them.",
  "description": "The two biggest compositions inside `heca/src/chrome/mod.rs` (4960 lines, host logic and UI in one file), and the ones carrying the hand-rolled text measuring this feature exists to end.\n\n## What exists\n\n- `build_pane_header()` :782 — title + the configured `PaneAction` buttons, each wired by hand (tooltip + hint + intent). `pane_action_spec()` :549 maps a `PaneAction` to (glyph, `WmAction`, label, focus-first) and stays the source of truth for what a button *is*.\n- `build_pane_info_bar()` :323 — icon+text segments (location, app name, git branch/status) with a **hand-rolled overflow budget** at :391: it measures with its own `char_w = font * 0.6` — a copy of `MONO_ADVANCE_RATIO` — computes the overflow in characters and left-ellipsises one designated segment through `truncate_path_left()` :286.\n- `build_pane_viewport_widgets()` :906 — the per-pane scrollbar + badge.\n- The same truncation exists a third and fourth time: `truncate_sidebar_git_branch()` :1428 (a fixed `SIDEBAR_GIT_BRANCH_MAX_CHARS` cap) and, as of F003/P085/T358, inside the command palette.\n\n## Blocked on the library owning text\n\n`Label` has **no truncation** — recorded as an open gap in AGENTS.md and never filed as a task, which is exactly how four hand-rolled copies came to exist. File and land `Label` truncation (`End` / `Start` ellipsis, measured once) in **F004** first; then the info bar's budget becomes \"give each segment its box and let the labels fit\", and `truncate_path_left` / `truncate_sidebar_git_branch` / the palette's copy all delete.\n\n## What to build\n\n- A **segment bar** component: an ordered list of (glyph, text) segments, one of them nominated as the shrinkable one, laid out by `Flex` with the labels doing their own fitting. No character arithmetic at the call site.\n- A **pane header** component composing it with the action buttons from P087's action-button component.\n- Both consumed by `chrome/mod.rs` in the same task that extracts them; the old functions go.\n\n## Behaviors to preserve\n\nPixel-identical bars and headers; the header rebuild cadence (`chrome_signature` / the width bucketing at :748 that keeps a resize from thrashing the rebuild) unchanged; per-pane header trees keep their own hint-id ranges and `remove_range` on rebuild; tooltips keep resolving through the action **name** so a rebind still updates them.",
