      "priority": 1,
      "shortName": "the-segment-bar-labels-fit-the",
      "title": "The segment bar: labels fit themselves, and four hand-rolled truncations die",
      "status": "planned",
      "description": "The pane info bar, extracted — and with it the character arithmetic this whole feature exists to end.\n\n## What exists\n\n`heca/src/chrome/mod.rs`:\n- `build_pane_info_bar()` :323 — icon+text segments (location, app name, git branch, git status), assembled inline.\n- Its **overflow budget** :391 — measures with its own `char_w = font * 0.6` (a hand-copy of `MONO_ADVANCE_RATIO`), sums the segment text, estimates a per-segment overhead of `font * 2.5`, computes the overflow in **characters**, and left-ellipsises the one designated segment through `truncate_path_left()` :286.\n- The same truncation, a third time: `truncate_sidebar_git_branch()` :1428 (fixed `SIDEBAR_GIT_BRANCH_MAX_CHARS` cap), used by the workspaces dock.\n- A fourth, from F003/P085/T358: the command palette's own `fit()`.\n- The rebuild cadence depends on this measure: the header signature buckets width (`w_bucket`, :748) so jitter does not thrash the rebuild while a real resize re-truncates.\n\n## Blocked on\n\n**`Label` must own truncation first** (F004 — file it; AGENTS.md records it as an open gap and it was never a task, which is exactly how four copies happened). Once a `Label` fits itself to its box, the bar becomes \"give each segment its box, nominate the shrinkable one\" and the arithmetic goes.\n\n## What to build\n\nA **segment bar** component: an ordered list of `(glyph, text)` segments with one nominated as shrinkable, laid out by `Flex`, each label fitting itself. No character counting at the call site, no `char_w`, no `truncate_path_left`.\n\nThen delete: the budget block at :391, `truncate_path_left`, `truncate_sidebar_git_branch` (its callers ask the component/label instead), and the palette's `fit()`.\n\n## Test\n\nHeadless paint: with a wide box every segment is drawn whole; with a narrow box **only** the nominated segment is cut, it ends in an ellipsis, and the others are untouched. Assert the drawn text, not a flag — a `grow` flag once passed while the layout was visibly broken (F004 lesson).\n\n## Behaviors to preserve\n\nPixel-identical bars; the location segment keeps **left** ellipsis (a path reads from its tail) while a label cuts at the end; the width bucketing that guards the rebuild cadence stays; per-pane header trees keep their own hint-id ranges.",
